{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}],"externalID":"GrafluentCollections","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","title":"GrafluentCollections"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"import GrafluentCollections","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and can be imported on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import GrafluentCollections","","var scores: FenwickTree = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]","print(scores.prefixSum(through: 3))  \/\/ 9","print(scores.sum(in: 2 ..< 6))       \/\/ 19"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Values-not-references","level":3,"text":"Values, not references","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every collection is a copy-on-write struct. Assigning one copies nothing until one of the copies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is mutated; then only that copy pays, once, and the other keeps its elements:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let original: BTree = [1, 2, 3]","var copy = original","copy.insert(4)","Array(original)   \/\/ [1, 2, 3]","Array(copy)       \/\/ [1, 2, 3, 4]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices of a tree live in flat arrays linked by integer indices rather than in a class per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, so a copy is a few array copies and a traversal reads memory almost in order. The API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"follows the standard library and Swift Collections: the sorted sets are "},{"code":"SetAlgebra","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"random-access collections indexed by rank, the dictionaries take "},{"code":"subscript(_:default:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range trees are collections of their values."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Traps-and-checked-spellings","level":3,"text":"Traps and checked spellings","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A plain spelling traps when its precondition fails, like an "},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" subscript out of range: it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fast path, for callers who know the precondition holds. Beside it, a "},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" spelling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws a typed error instead, one of those in "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" turns it into an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let primes: AVLTree = [2, 3, 5, 7]","primes[2]                    \/\/ 5","try primes[checked: 9]       \/\/ throws IndexOutOfRange"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A mutation that would break a structure’s invariant, such as joining two treaps whose elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interleave, throws on its plain spelling and changes nothing. Where the standard library’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collections return an optional (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(_:)"},{"text":", a dictionary’s subscript, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"min()"},{"text":"), these do too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Grafluent-conversions","level":3,"text":"Grafluent conversions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A collection whose shape is a tree converts to the Grafluent type of that shape: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"text":", with an initializer on the Grafluent type that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"costs O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":") once. Structures whose shape is a general graph, such as decision diagrams and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automata, offer a view that is a Grafluent graph without copying. Either way, Grafluent’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms, drawings and file formats run over the collection; its own operations never go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the conversion. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"},{"text":" shows the round trip.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Modules","level":3,"text":"Modules","type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Group"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Modules","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Search trees"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (AVL, red–black and splay trees, treaps), ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (B-trees), ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (skip lists)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tries","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/tries","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" (tries over any sequence of symbols, radix and Patricia trees, Aho–Corasick automata)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Suffix structures","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/suffixstructures"},{"type":"text","text":" (suffix arrays with LCP, suffix trees, suffix automata)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decision diagrams"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (reduced ordered BDDs, zero-suppressed ZDDs)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Range and spatial trees","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/rangetrees"},{"type":"text","text":" (Fenwick trees, segment trees with lazy propagation, interval trees), "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/spatialtrees"},{"type":"text","text":" (k-d trees, quadtrees, octrees)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sequences and persistence","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/ropes","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (ropes: sequences as balanced trees of chunks), "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (path-copying weight-balanced trees that keep every version)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Caches"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/caches","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (LRU caches)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shared"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"overridingTitle":"CollectionErrors","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"CollectionErrors","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors"},{"type":"text","text":": the errors the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" spellings throw, re-exported by every module that throws them"}]}]]],"type":"table"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"],"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Convert a collection’s shape to a Grafluent graph, then lay it out, write it or run an algorithm","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/seeingacollectionasagraph","title":"Seeing a collection as a graph","kind":"article"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/btrees":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTrees"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","title":"BTrees"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/tries":{"type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"Tries","type":"codeVoice"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/tries","title":"Tries","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/tries"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/caches":{"title":"Caches","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/caches","url":"https:\/\/ty